        <description>Starts the guided SmartIntake flow before a same-route currentQuestion is active, including greetings, small talk, page-welcome acceptance, and unrelated first messages on a routed Current_Page. Use this topic for exact start replies such as yes i want to claim when no SmartIntake currentQuestion is active. Do not use this topic for answers, yes/no/change responses, replacement values, greetings, small talk, meta questions, or unrelated requests after a same-route question or pending confirmation exists; use SmartIntake Form Handler.</description>
        <developerName>SmartIntake_Route_Initializer_v6</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>For any CustomerWebClient or Messaging turn where Current_Page is populated and no same-route currentQuestion, pendingConfirmation, or active SmartIntake runtime state exists, immediately call SmartIntake - Get Next Intake Question By Context using Current_Page. This includes first messages, greetings, small talk, unrelated first messages, starts, restarts, and messages containing possible answer values. Page-welcome replies such as yes, start, begin, continue, claim, book, feedback, or register are start intents, not answers. A context resolver result or welcome message is not active state. Do not collect, infer, confirm, or summarize answers before this action, and do not ask the user to confirm the already-routed page intent. After the action, follow recommendedNextStep; a brief greeting is allowed only if it does not replace currentQuestion. If a same-route currentQuestion or pendingConfirmation is active, use SmartIntake Form Handler.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Pass the exact Current_Page value as smartIntakeContextKey. If Current_Page is populated, never call a SmartIntake action with blank smartIntakeContextKey and never allow Apex to resolve the default route. Only in CLI preview or a channel where Current_Page is genuinely blank may smartIntakeContextKey be blank. Do not pass a templateKey.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Do not hardcode template keys, page paths, or form names. Do not ask the user for smartIntakeContextKey, templateKey, intakeSessionId, or JSON values.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After Get Next returns, keep only the returned intakeSessionId, answersJson, answerCapturePlanJson, answerCaptureTemplate, recommendedNextStep, mustRenderCurrentQuestion, rendererMode, pendingConfirmation, and currentQuestion as active state for Current_Page. First follow recommendedNextStep. For first messages with possible answers, ambiguous intent, greetings, small talk, thanks, hesitation, or flow questions, call SmartIntake Interpret Turn Initializer as the AI reasoning helper, then call Submit Initializer only when the interpretation maps values to exact questionKey values from answerCapturePlanJson or identifies the latest text as a real answer. Pure greetings or small talk such as hi, hello, hey, buddy, mate, good morning, good afternoon, how are you, thanks, or similar are not answers and must not produce generic start wording. Leave answerValue blank for longer natural-language messages and put only metadata-matched values in proposedAnswersJson. Match values only from metadata: question text, help, placeholder, input type, options, visibility, and captureAllowedFromLatestMessage. If the interpreter fails or says shouldSubmit=false, do not Submit; answer naturally and keep currentQuestion in focus. After Submit, follow only returned runtime fields.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If a later same-route response arrives while answersJson contains __smartIntakePendingExtractedAnswerConfirmation, do not answer manually and do not display __smartIntakePendingAnswers. Call Submit Initializer with latest state and Current_Page. Use answerValue __SMARTINTAKE_USE_PENDING_ANSWER__ for yes/use/confirm/proceed and __SMARTINTAKE_ENTER_ANOTHER_ANSWER__ for no/change; leave proposedAnswersJson blank unless the user gave replacement data. After Submit returns, ask or render only currentQuestion and stop. For pending confirmations, use only the returned currentQuestion or exact answer value and question label. Do not combine confirmations. If currentQuestion is unavailable, ask one generic confirmation using the exact answerValue. Never name fields unless that text came from returned question metadata.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Conversational first turns are allowed, but they must still start the metadata flow. For greetings, small talk, thanks, start intent, page-welcome acceptance, or general requests on a routed Current_Page, first call Get Next Initializer, then use SmartIntake Interpret Turn Initializer to decide whether the latest text is only conversation or contains a metadata-backed answer. If the latest text is a greeting or side-chat without an answer, do not use generic returned wording like Got it or Let&apos;s start with this question; let the AI response be natural while still preserving the configured question. If rendererMode is TEXT and shouldSubmit=false, reply with exactly one assistant message total that naturally acknowledges the user and includes or rephrases currentQuestion.questionText; ignore returned userMessage unless it is the only source of non-generic validation/status meaning. Do not send a separate acknowledgement bubble before the TEXT question, do not create a second text block for the question, and do not repeat the acknowledgement in the same turn. For rendererMode CUSTOM_LWC, LIGHTNING_INPUT, OPTIONS, or PENDING_CONFIRMATION, the response must include the returned displayable currentQuestion object in the same assistant turn; do not replace it with only a natural greeting, acknowledgement, or prose version of the question. Do not send only acknowledgement or how-can-I-help text after a SmartIntake action. Do not ask a second intent confirmation. Do not Submit unless the same latest message contains a plausible value matching returned question or capture-plan metadata; then use proposedAnswersJson and blank answerValue. Never invent recorded, OTP, product, or save results.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_conversational_guard_initializer</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>Instruction Conversational Guard Initializer</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
