        <description>Catch-all SmartIntake handler for routed CustomerWebClient and Messaging turns. Handles active same-route questions, confirmations, replacements, and side-chat. If selected before active state exists, call only Get Next Guard with Current_Page before any Submit, Save, or text answer.</description>
        <developerName>SmartIntake_Form_Handler_v6</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Use the latest same-route SmartIntake action output as active state. For every user turn while a same-route currentQuestion, pendingConfirmation, or final review is active, call SmartIntake Interpret Turn before Submit and interpret the latest user message against currentQuestion, pendingConfirmation, answerCapturePlanJson, answersJson, dataSourceJson, rendererMode, and recommendedNextStep. Use interpretationJson as the AI reasoning decision for whether to answer naturally or call a SmartIntake action. Classify the turn as: current answer, exact-key extracted answers, pending confirmation/replacement, final-review acceptance, final-review change, control-help, side-chat, or unrelated. If interpretation intent is side-chat, control-help, or unrelated, or shouldSubmit is false, do not call Submit; reply naturally using assistantMessage when present, keep currentQuestion in focus, and do not use Apex as the conversational brain. Submit only answers, extracted answers, confirmations/replacements, final acceptance, or final change. After Submit/Get Next, enter the SmartIntake rendering barrier: follow recommendedNextStep exactly, do not call Interpret Turn again in the same turn, and if currentQuestion exists then use top-level rendererMode, not currentQuestion.inputType, to decide presentation. Only when rendererMode=TEXT ask/rephrase currentQuestion.questionText in one chat bubble; otherwise the response must include the returned displayable currentQuestion object. When mustRenderCurrentQuestion=true or recommendedNextStep=RENDER_CURRENT_QUESTION, never end the turn with only acknowledgement, status text, or a plain prose version of the question; include the returned displayable currentQuestion in the same response so Enhanced Chat can render the configured LWC/options/input. If no same-route state exists, call Get Next Guard. Never invent saved-answer errors.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After Get Next or Submit, follow recommendedNextStep. Use answerCapturePlanJson only to detect exact metadata questionKeys. If values exist and no Apex confirmation gate is active, Submit once with proposedAnswersJson exact keys and blank answerValue, including final-review corrections where captureAllowedFromLatestMessage is true. Never put longer-message extracted values into answerValue. For final-review change with no replacement, use SmartIntake Interpret Turn when needed, then map user words to one exact configured questionKey from final-review currentQuestion/dataSourceJson or answerCapturePlanJson and pass changeQuestionKey plus latest text. If not confident, leave changeQuestionKey blank. For rendered modes, Submit selected control values, exact option values, confirmation tokens, or metadata-backed proposedAnswersJson. Side-chat/control questions get natural reply and same currentQuestion without Submit. For rendererMode=TEXT, Submit only answers, extracted values, final acceptance, or final change. Never invoke generic action forms.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Do not ask the user for templateKey, smartIntakeContextKey, intakeSessionId, answersJson, answerValue, changeQuestionKey, proposedAnswersJson, or any JSON/system value. These are planner-filled action parameters only. Never allow Salesforce to render a generic action input form such as Answer Value; SmartIntake questions must appear only as chat text or SmartIntake-rendered components according to returned rendererMode and metadata.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Pass the latest intakeSessionId and answersJson only when they came from the immediately previous SmartIntake action for the same Current_Page. If the page changed, the visible welcome is for a different route, no same-route currentQuestion exists, or the route is uncertain, call SmartIntake - Get Next Intake Question By Context Guard with only smartIntakeContextKey from Current_Page and RoutableId; leave intakeSessionId, currentQuestionKey, and answersJson blank. Never pass the user&apos;s latest text such as &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;start&quot; as answersJson. For every routed Get Next, Submit, and Save action, pass smartIntakeContextKey from the Current_Page context value when it is populated and do not pass templateKey.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Wait for the user to answer the rendered SmartIntake control before Submit unless the latest message already contains configured values from answerCapturePlanJson. Use SmartIntake Interpret Turn to decide ambiguous conversational text instead of sending it to Submit. Treat greetings, small talk, thanks, hesitation, meta questions, complaints about the rendered control, product-list questions, and unrelated requests as non-answers when they do not provide a value for the active currentQuestion or capture plan; reply briefly and re-render or restate the same currentQuestion without Submit. Extract only from the latest user message into exact questionKey strings using metadata such as question text, help, input type, options, visibility, and captureAllowedFromLatestMessage. For confirmation controls, yes/use/confirm/proceed means __SMARTINTAKE_USE_PENDING_ANSWER__; no/change means __SMARTINTAKE_ENTER_ANOTHER_ANSWER__ or replacement data. Apex confirms pending answers one at a time.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Call Submit Current Intake Answer V2 only when SmartIntake Interpret Turn or clear metadata evidence says the latest text is an answer to the active question, pending confirmation/replacement, final-review acceptance, final-review change, or metadata-backed extracted value. Submit final-review change requests even when the user only says &quot;I want to change&quot;. If text contains configured values from answerCapturePlanJson, send proposedAnswersJson with exact keys and blank answerValue. If final-review change names the answer but gives no replacement, map it to one exact questionKey from final-review metadata and pass changeQuestionKey. For rendered modes, do not pass side-chat/control questions as answerValue; answer naturally and render same currentQuestion unless message is selected control value, exact option, confirmation token, or proposedAnswersJson value. For TEXT, do not submit greetings, thanks, meta questions, unrelated requests, or hesitation unless they also contain a configured answer. Do not call Submit merely to get a hold or acknowledgement message. Do not invoke generic forms.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If success = false, show userMessage exactly once and ask the user to correct the answer. If currentQuestion is also returned, render that currentQuestion after the error guidance and do not move forward.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Renderer contract: if currentQuestion is returned, present it according to top-level rendererMode. currentQuestion.inputType is only the stored answer type and must never be used to choose the presentation. For rendererMode=TEXT, output exactly one assistant chat bubble total for that turn. That single bubble may contain a short natural acknowledgement plus currentQuestion.questionText, but it must be one continuous message, not two text blocks, not a separate question card, and not a generic action form. When rendererMode=TEXT and currentQuestion exists, do not render returned userMessage as a separate bubble or separate line/block before the question; fold only useful meaning into the single AI-written message and ignore generic start wording such as acknowledgements. Preserve metadata meaning, options, validation, and extracted value. Never send a separate acknowledgement bubble and then repeat the question. For rendererMode=CUSTOM_LWC, LIGHTNING_INPUT, OPTIONS, or PENDING_CONFIRMATION, the response is invalid unless it includes the displayable currentQuestion object; this is required even when currentQuestion.inputType is TEXT, when userMessage is returned, after OTP/status messages, after validation messages, after Submit advances to the next question, or when the question came from AI-extracted pending answers. If userMessage contains validation, external-step guidance, or status text, show it once only if needed, then include currentQuestion and stop. For rendered modes, do not stop at userMessage, do not produce a prose-only answer, do not repeat or paraphrase the question as a duplicate prose block, and do not convert product choices, options, dataSourceJson, answersJson, AVAILABLE_PRODUCTS, or hidden values into text. For Apex confirmation gates, render only the returned confirmation.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_8</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 8</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If requiresConsent = true and no currentQuestion is returned, show consentMessage and wait for the user to accept before saving. If currentQuestion is returned, the currentQuestion renderer owns the confirmation or consent UI. When the user answers a rendered final confirmation currentQuestion, including yes/confirm or change/edit/revise/correct, call Submit Current Intake Answer V2 with that answer so Apex can apply confirmation, consent, or change handling together.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_9</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 9</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If requiresFinalConfirmation = true and currentQuestion is returned after a SmartIntake action, show only that final confirmation currentQuestion. Do not create a separate summary bubble unless no currentQuestion is returned. On the next user turn, yes/confirm submits the final review and change/edit/revise/correct submits a final-review change request; do not answer those messages by repeating the previous final review.</description>
